{title: 272 - Give Me the Bible}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #272 • GIVE ME THE BIBLE • 11.10.12.10.11.10.11.10}
{lyricist: Priscilla J. Owens}
{composer: E. S. Lorenz}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 272}
{meta: tune GIVE ME THE BIBLE}
{meta: meter 11.10.12.10.11.10.11.10}
{meta: category Holy Scriptures - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Give me the Bible, star of gladness [C/G]gleaming,
[F#dim]To cheer the wand'rer [G]lone [C/G]and tempest [G]tossed;
[G]No storm can hide that radiance peaceful [F#dim]beaming,
[G]Since Jesus came [C/G]to [F#dim]seek and save the [G]lost.
[C/G]Give me the Bible, holy [G]message [C/G]shining;
[F#dim]Thy light shall guide [G]me in the narrow way;
[Bm]Precept [D7]and promise, [G]law and love combining,
[G]Till night shall vanish in eternal [Bm]day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G]Give me [Am]the Bible--
[G]holy message shining,
[G]Thy light shall guide [C/G]me
[F#dim]in the narrow way.
[G]Precept and promise,
[C/G]law and love [G]combining,
[F#dim]'Til night shall [G]vanish
[G]in eternal day.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Give me the Bible
[F#dim]when my heart [G]is [C/G]broken,
[G]When sin and grief [F#dim]have
[G]filled my [C/G]soul [F#dim]with fear,
[C/G]Give me the [G]precious
[F#dim]words by Jesus [G]spoken,
[Bm]Hold [D7]up [G]faith's lamp
[G]to show my Savior [Bm]near.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Give me the Bible,
[F#dim]all my steps [G]enlighten,
[G]Teach me the danger
[G]of these [C/G]realms [F#dim]below,
[C/G]That lamp of safety,
[F#dim]o'er the gloom [G]shall brighten,
[Bm]That [D7]light [G]alone
[G]the path of peace can [Bm]show.
{end_of_verse}
